      ],
      "content": "TRING                 WESTERN ROAD SP 91 SW                                         (North side) 4/113                                   Nos. 92, and 94 - -                                       II Semi-detached pair of villas. Early C19. Stucco with hipped slate roofs. A pair of 2-storeys, double-pile plan, adjoining classical villas set back  from  road,  facing  S.  Each  is  a  3-windows  wide  symmetrical composition with plinth, clasping corner pilasters, narrow eaves band below wide plastered eaves soffit with paired brackets moulded surrounds to recessed sash windows with 8/8 panes of Crown glass (taller windows on ground floor), and central entrance. 6-panel door with semi-circular fanlight in round headed doorway, under projecting Tuscan porch with tapering  columns,  full  entablature,  and  blocking  course.  End-wall chimneys. Listing NGR: SP9182711096"
    }
